   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Memory ladder, fastest to slowest: on-die SRAM (MBs) → HBM on the package (GBs at TB/s) → host DRAM over PCIe (TBs, ~50–100× slower to reach) → NVMe.\nWeights and the KV cache sit in HBM because decode re-reads them for every token.",
   "originalText": "Memory ladder, fastest to slowest: on-die SRAM (MBs) → HBM on the package (GBs at TB/s) → host DRAM over PCIe (TBs, ~50–100× slower to reach) → NVMe.\nWeights and the KV cache sit in HBM because decode re-reads them for every token.",
   "fontSize": 17,
   "fontFamily": 5,
